       "url": "adenoma/#decision-5"
      }
     ],
     "positions": [
      {
       "source": "EASL 2016",
       "key": "pm27085809",
       "says": "Names exophytic protrusion but builds no rule around it; its triggers are persistent size over 5 cm or growth of 20% or more of diameter, irrespective of subtype.",
       "locator": "What we are not sure about #11; Gate 4 · Standard 'Treat a lesion that is persistently larger than 5 cm…'"
      },
      {
       "source": "Bieze 2014",
       "key": "pm24760723",
       "says": "The only cohort fitting a bleeding cut-point found 35 mm (5.4% below, 53% above), but was retrospective, used a 5 cm resection protocol and found no beta-catenin adenoma; its positional figures could not be confirmed and were withdrawn.",
       "locator": "Gate 4 · Reasonable 'Where a woman's adenoma sits between 4 and 5 cm…' (caveat and note); What we are not sure about #11"
      },
      {
       "source": "Deneve 2009",
       "key": "pm19130136",
       "says": "The 124-patient series fitted its size dichotomy at 7 cm, yet its authors recommended resecting above 4 cm; no guideline adopted that.",
       "locator": "Gate 4 · Standard 'State where the 5 cm number comes from…' (and note)"
      },
      {
       "source": "WHO 6th ed., as reviewed (2026)",
       "key": "pm42678415",
       "says": "Exon 3 adenomas are resected or ablated whatever their size and sonic hedgehog adenomas bleed even below 5 cm; the roadmap calls both expert assertion without a cited cohort.",
       "locator": "Gate 4 · Reasonable 'Where a woman's adenoma sits between 4 and 5 cm…'"
      }
     ],
     "divergence": "No guideline endorses a composite trigger or operating below 5 cm on position alone, the positional effect sizes once offered in support have been withdrawn as unverified, and the only fitted cut-point cannot exclude subtype as the real driver.",
     "proposal": "Undecided by design: the roadmap says this cannot be decided until someone reads the 35 mm cohort's positional analysis directly. Meanwhile, record position and vascularity alongside diameter and treat a 4-5 cm lesion as a board judgement on subtype, position and trajectory; the composite trigger stands only as a grade D proposal.",
     "proposal_locator": "Decisions this programme still has to make #7; What we are not sure about #11; Gate 4 · Standard 'State where the 5 cm number comes from…' and Reasonable 'Where a woman's adenoma sits between 4 and 5 cm…'",
     "rationale": "This item cannot be decided yet, and that is now the honest answer. The positional and vascular effect sizes this page previously quoted in support could not be confirmed in the full-text read and have been withdrawn; what the supporting paper does establish is a fitted cut-point at 35 mm with bleeding in 5.4% below against 53% above, in a retrospective cohort whose own protocol used 5 cm to decide which lesions were resected, with grades I to III pooled, no beta-catenin adenoma identified in 195 lesions and 48% unclassifiable. Adopting a composite trigger would mean operating on some lesions below 5 cm, which no guideline endorses. Before deciding, someone should read that paper's positional analysis directly and report the numbers.",
     "audit": "Registry: for every haemorrhage, which trigger features were present and whether they had been recorded prospectively.",
     "web": "adenoma/#question-HCA-D7"
    },
    {
     "id": "HCA-D8",
     "set": "roadmap",
     "title": "Does the transplant protocol's S45 and exon 7/8 restriction stand as written?",
     "question": "Does the transplant protocol's S45 and exon 7/8 restriction stand as written?",
     "kind": "governance",
     "status": "OPEN — not yet decided",
     "where": [
      {
       "label": "10 · Assess transplant eligibility",
       "url": "adenoma/#decision-10"
